"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24929-econclark","name":"econclark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-23T06:24:58-08:00","id":1468679,"title":"","content":"I would also recommend &quot;The Way of the House Husband&quot; for a more comedic inspiration for an Assassins game. It's a manga about a former Yakuza who retires and gets married. He uses his various skills from being a criminal to be the perfect stay at home spouse to his business woman wife, including monologues about honer among thieves while dealing with supermarket sales and cooking duels with rival gang members to see whose dish gets more likes on social media.<br /> <br /> And for a weirder inspiration go with Hit Monkey from Marvel. Its about a monkey that becomes a hit man after his tribe is killed. Not a super science monkey or anything just a monkey. I would run it as a Talented Monkey, which opens up all sorts of possibility's.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27184-darrendalca","name":"DarrenDalca","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27184_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}